{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF20-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md && printf '\\\\n--- FF21 ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,280p' history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF21-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md && printf '\\\\n--- FF22 archive contents ---\\\\n' && tar -tzf history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF22-finite-range-tracial-corner-fullness.tar.gz | sed -n '1,80p'\"","aggregated_output":"# FF20 live closeout adversarial review\n\n## Decision\n\n**Accepted at the packet's stated conditional scope.**  The downloaded\nAristotle archive is retained in quarantine as\n`FF20-stabilizer-support-corner-instantiation.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`5097660af857a567d1a2ef5a0f415a7377f358528459651af95d1c1246d548fb`) and\nwas extracted only under `FF20-extracted/`.  The only integrated source is\n`formalization_finite_fibers/FiniteFiber/ActualStabilizerSupportCorner.lean`,\nwhich is byte-identical to the candidate.  Remote metadata, source context,\nREADME/HANDOFF differences, and the remote summary's commit/push assertion\nwere not integrated.\n\n## Scope audit\n\nThe module connects the actual full-Pauli local system and FF19's conditional\nquasilocal/GNS interface to the already checked support-corner result.  It\nadds no axiom, `sorry`, `admit`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, or `implemented_by`\ndeclaration.  It does not modify the manuscript.\n\n### Proved in the live package\n\n- `QuasilocalEmbedding.wordElement`, `embed_eq_wordElement`, `wordElement_one`,\n  `wordElement_mul`, and `wordHom` give a region-independent unital\n  multiplicative image of a `FullPauliWord`.\n- `QuasilocalStabilizerState.stabilizerRepresentation`, `stabilizerAction`,\n  `isSelfAdjoint_stabilizerRepresentation`,\n  `stabilizerRepresentation_gnsVector`, and `stabilizerRepresentation_mem`\n  give the represented actual stabilizer action, its self-adjointness, GNS\n  vector invariance, and membership from the stated local-algebra containment.\n- `actualStabilizerSystem_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit` concludes\n  `SupportCornerConclusion M q W.gnsVector` from exactly\n  `W`, `M`, `hM`, finite `T`, `hmonotone`, `hstrong`, and\n  `C : GNSOrbitConditions M q W.gnsVector`.\n- `actualStabilizerSystem_canonicalSupportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit` has\n  the same inputs except that it uses the constructed decreasing strong limit\n  and therefore has no `hstrong` premise.\n- `actualStabilizerSystem_central_witness_of_gnsOrbit` restates the target:\n  for `hz : IsCentralProjection M z` and `hz_nonzero : z != 0`, it returns\n  `IsFiniteProjection M (z * q) /\\\\ z * q != 0 /\\\\ IsSubprojection (z * q) z`.\n- `actualStabilizerSystem_semifinite_of_gnsOrbit` is the corresponding\n  conditional `IsSemifinite M` corollary.\n\n### Still conditional / not proved\n\nThe theorem does not construct the quasilocal completion or global state\n(`Q`, `W`), the ambient regional von Neumann algebra and containment `hM`, an\nexhausting finite subgroup sequence `T`, a noncanonical strong-limit proof\n`hstrong`, or `GNSOrbitConditions` (in particular the regional/product-orbit\ndata, fullness, and corner traciality).  Thus it does **not** establish that\nthese inputs follow from the manuscript short-range condition; it also makes\nno direct-integral or type-III claim.  This is the packet-required conditional\ninstantiation, not a completion of the global model.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `lake build FiniteFiber.ActualStabilizerSupportCorner` -- passed.\n- `lake build` -- passed.\n- `lake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean` -- passed; existing audited declarations\n  report only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- `#print axioms` for every public FF20 definition/theorem -- only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder scan of the candidate module -- no matches.\n\n## Adversarial findings\n\nNo blocking finding.  The potential overclaim -- treating the FF19 interface\nor the GNS-orbit conditions as constructed consequences of a short-range\nmodel -- is avoided in both the declarations and module documentation.\nResidual mathematical risk is precisely the unconstructed global hypotheses\nlisted above; successful compilation does not discharge them.\n\n--- FF21 ---\n# FF21 live closeout adversarial review\n\n## Decision\n\n**Accepted at the packet's stated conditional scope.**  The completed remote\nsnapshot is retained only in quarantine as\n`FF21-finite-range-support-corner-construction.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`6e7d73c1fbae016aad64c39ce1cf5dbeab1f61befd23ea45f5695a7f2deb8466`) and\nwas extracted only under `FF21-extracted/`.  No build, dependency update, or\nother executable action was run in that snapshot.\n\nOnly the reviewed candidate module was integrated into the live package as\n`formalization_finite_fibers/FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction.lean`.\nIt is byte-identical to the quarantined candidate.  `FiniteFiber.lean` was\nchanged only to import that module and its already-live FF20 dependency\n`ActualStabilizerSupportCorner`.  Remote metadata, README/HANDOFF differences,\nand `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md` were not integrated.  The manuscript was not\nmodified.\n\n## Exact checked interface and status\n\n### Proved\n\n- `FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem Site` packages a surjective enumeration,\n  finite self-containing neighbourhoods, a consistent commuting involutive\n  `FullPauliWord.StabilizerGeneratorData`, and the exact finite-range premise\n  `forall g in generators, exists s, g.label.support subset neighborhood s`.\n- `region`, `exhaustion`, `region_mono`, `mem_region`, and\n  `exists_region_superset` give a finite monotone exhaustion.  The\n  finite-range-specific conclusion is\n  `generator_supportedIn_region`.\n- `localStabilizer`, `localStabilizerFintype`, `localStabilizer_mono`,\n  `exists_mem_localStabilizer`, and `iSup_localStabilizer` give the increasing\n  finite local stabilizer sequence.  `LocallyGenerated` is recorded as an\n  additional condition; only\n  `closure_localGenerators_le_regionStabilizer` is derived from the stated\n  data.\n- Given the existing explicit interface inputs\n  `W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q`, `M`, and `hM`,\n  `supportProjectionSequence` proves the decreasing represented support\n  projections.  `cornerProjection` uses the already checked project-local\n  `decreasingProjectionStrongLimit`; its strong convergence, membership and\n  projection property, GNS-vector fixedness, and nonzero conclusion are\n  respectively `stronglyTendsTo_cornerProjection`,\n  `cornerProjection_isProjectionIn`, `cornerProjection_gnsVector`, and\n  `cornerProjection_ne_zero`.\n- With the still-explicit\n  `C : GNSOrbitConditions M (R.cornerProjection W) W.gnsVector`, the exact\n  target-facing declarations are\n  `finiteRange_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit` and\n  `finiteRange_central_witness_of_gnsOrbit`.  The latter returns, for each\n  nonzero central `z`, a finite nonzero subprojection\n  `z * R.cornerProjection W` below `z`.\n\n### Partial / conditional\n\nThe packet's geometric/operator-algebraic target is met: it supplies the\nfinite local sequence and a constructed nonzero candidate corner projection.\nThe final support-corner conclusion remains conditional on the already\nexplicit quasilocal completion/state interface `Q`, `W`, local containment\n`hM`, and `GNSOrbitConditions` (notably product-orbit fullness and corner\ntraciality).  The strong-limit route is a project-local supporting theorem,\nnot a new axiom or an unproved premise.\n\n### Blocked\n\nNo Lean obstruction remains for FF21.  The global analytic inputs above are\nnot blocked proof holes in this module; they are deliberately supplied\npremises outside the packet's scope.\n\n### Failed\n\nNo failed claim was integrated.  In particular, FF21 does not claim that\nfinite range supplies local-code equality, a trace, fullness, a type\nclassification, or a no-type-III theorem.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `lake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction` -- passed.\n- `lake build FiniteFiber` -- passed.\n- `lake build` -- passed.\n- `lake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean` -- passed.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan of the candidate -- no match for\n  `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or\n  `native_decide`.\n- `#print axioms` was run for every public FF21 theorem; each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- `git diff --check` -- passed.\n\n## Adversarial findings and residual risk\n\nNo blocking defect found.  The main potential overclaim was that finite range\nalone might prove the converse local-generator equality or the analytic\nGNS-orbit hypotheses.  The module isolates the former as `LocallyGenerated`\nand keeps the latter in the theorem premises.  Compilation and axiom auditing\nverify formal consistency only; they do not construct the quasilocal state or\ndischarge those analytic assumptions.\n\n## Cleanup\n\nThe quarantine archive and extracted snapshot are intentional retained raw\nresponse records.  Existing repository-wide dirty and untracked material was\npreserved.  No commit, push, dependency fetch, or manuscript change occurred.\n\n--- FF22 archive contents ---\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/lakefile.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/lean-toolchain\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/lake-manifest.json\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/StabilizerFiniteFiber.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FiniteNestedPauli.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/GNSOrbit.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FiniteNestedTensorState.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionPauliMatrices.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FiniteQubitMatrix.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionQubitAlgebra.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FiniteLocalGroupSupport.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/Basic.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/StabilizerSequence.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FinitePauliStabilizer.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FiniteTensorMatrixChain.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/QuasilocalStateGNSInterface.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/VectorCorner.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/OneSitePauliNormalForm.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/ActualStabilizerSupportCorner.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FullPauliLattice.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FinitePauli.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FiniteStabilizerTrace.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FiniteDensity.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/GNSVector.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FullPauliDirectedLocalSystem.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/StrongSupport.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FiniteLocalPauli.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FullPauliSupportLocality.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/SequentialLocalFunctional.lean\naristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/F