{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'set -euo pipefail\nresponse_dir=history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses\nremote_root=$(find \"$response_dir/FF23-extracted\" -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -type d | head -n 1)\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- candidate source ---'\nsed -n '1,360p' \\\"\"'$remote_root/FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeNoTypeIII.lean\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- remote summary ---'\nsed -n '1,240p' \\\"\"'$remote_root/ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- candidate forbidden scan ---'\nrg -n '\\\\b(sorry|admit|axiom|opaque|unsafe|implemented_by|native_decide)\\\\b' \\\"\"'$remote_root/FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeNoTypeIII.lean\" || true\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- dependency hashes comparison ---'\nfor f in FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeTracialCorner.lean FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction.lean FiniteFiber/ActualStabilizerSupportCorner.lean FiniteFiber.lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean; do\n  printf '%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$f\"\n  sha256sum \"$f\" \"$remote_root/$f\" 2>/dev/null || true\ndone\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- remote vs live relevant dependency diffs ---'\ndiff -u FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeTracialCorner.lean \\\"\"'$remote_root/FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeTracialCorner.lean\" | sed -n '\"'1,220p' || true\n\"","aggregated_output":"--- candidate source ---\nimport FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeTracialCorner\n\n/-!\n# FF23 — finite-range stabilizer systems have no type-III central summand\n\nThis is the closing file of the packet.  It states and proves the manuscript's\nmain theorem (`thm:finite_projections_exist`, quoted as the Proposition of\nSection \"No Type III algebras in stabilizer systems\") in its robust\n*central-summand* form, for the GNS von Neumann algebra of a supplied\nconsistent **finite-range** stabilizer system:\n\n> for every nonzero central projection `z` of `M`, the summand `z M` contains a\n> nonzero finite projection.\n\nNothing new is assumed here beyond what FF20–FF22 already carry: the file only\napplies the already checked support-corner theorem\n(`FiniteFiber.SupportCornerConclusion`) to the concrete corner projection `q`\nconstructed in FF21 and shown in FF22 to be nonzero, full, and to carry a\nfaithful tracial corner state.\n\n## The two contracts, distinguished\n\nThere are exactly two forms of the theorem in this file.\n\n*Unconditional at the canonical algebra.*  For `M = M_Γ = π_ω(𝒜_loc)''`, the\nvon Neumann algebra generated by the represented local algebra on the GNS space\n(`QuasilocalStabilizerState.localVonNeumannAlgebra`, the bicommutant\nconstructed in FF22), the theorem\n`FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.central_summand_exists_nonzero_finiteProjection`\ncarries **no** hypothesis beyond the packet data itself:\n\n* `R : FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem Site` — a countable, locally finite lattice\n  with a consistent finite-range stabilizer system (FF21);\n* `Q : QuasilocalEmbedding Site A` — the quasilocal C-star completion of the\n  finite local qubit algebras (interface input, FF19/FF20);\n* `W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q` — the global stabilizer\n  state extending the compatible finite local states, i.e. the state asserted\n  by the manuscript's Proposition `prop:define_state` (interface input).\n\nGiven `R`, `Q`, `W` the conclusion is a theorem, with the corner projection `q`\n*constructed* and the finite witness in each summand exhibited explicitly as\n`z * q`.\n\n*Conditional at a general algebra.*  For an arbitrary von Neumann algebra `M`\non the GNS space the same conclusion is proved from the two premises which\nFF21/FF22 isolate and which are preserved here verbatim:\n\n* `hM` : `M` contains every represented finite local algebra (`𝒜 ⊆ M`);\n* `hgen` : `W.GeneratedByLocalAlgebra M`, i.e. `M ⊆ π_ω(𝒜_loc)''`.\n\nTogether they say exactly `M = M_Γ`; they are a definitional identification of\n`M`, not an analytic gap, and for the canonical `M_Γ` they are discharged,\nwhich is why the first contract is unconditional.\n\n## Scope, honestly stated\n\n* `Q` and `W` are *supplied* data.  This packet does not construct the\n  quasilocal C-star completion or the global state for an infinite lattice; the\n  finite-range geometry is non-vacuous\n  (`FiniteFiber.natAllZFiniteRangeSystem`, the all-`Z` code on `ℕ`) and the two\n  interfaces are separately non-vacuous\n  (`FiniteFiber.emptySiteQuasilocalEmbedding`,\n  `FiniteFiber.emptySiteQuasilocalStabilizerState`), but a simultaneous\n  instantiation of all three on an infinite lattice is *not* constructed here.\n  Accordingly the unconditional statement above is unconditional **relative to\n  the supplied interface data**, and is not a claim that the data exists.\n* The algebra treated is the full-lattice algebra `π_ω(𝒜_loc)''` (the case\n  `Γ = ℒ` of the manuscript's `M_Γ`), since that is the algebra for which\n  FF22 supplies the tracial corner.\n* Finiteness of a projection is the Murray–von Neumann notion of\n  `FiniteFiber.Basic` (`IsFiniteProjection`), and \"every nonzero central\n  summand contains a nonzero finite projection\" is `FiniteFiber.IsSemifinite`.\n  No trace-theoretic reformulation of semifiniteness is proved.\n\n## The type-III corollary (prose, deliberately not direct-integral)\n\nThe Lean statement below is the central-summand statement, plus its immediate\nformal restatement\n`FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection`:\nno nonzero central summand `z M` satisfies `SummandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection`,\ni.e. no nonzero central summand is *purely infinite in the projection sense*.\n\n**Prose corollary (not formalized).**  The absence of nonzero finite\nprojections is the defining feature of a type-III von Neumann algebra\n(Blackadar, III.1.4.2).  Hence, for a consistent finite-range stabilizer system\nwith the supplied quasilocal completion and global state, in a standard central\ndecomposition of `M_Γ` — that is, under the usual hypotheses making such a\ndecomposition available, namely a separable predual/separable GNS space and the\nmeasurable-field machinery of the central direct-integral decomposition — no\ncentral summand, and in particular no fibre factor occurring with positive\nmeasure, can be of type III.  This step is *prose only*: the requisite\nseparability and direct-integral API is not available in Mathlib and is not\ndeveloped in this packet, so no direct-integral or fibrewise type-classification\nstatement is asserted in Lean.  What is proved in Lean is exactly the\ncentral-summand statement, which is the form of the manuscript's theorem that\ndoes not need that machinery.\n-/\n\nnamespace FiniteFiber\n\nsection Abstract\n\nvariable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n\n/--\nThe projection-level form of \"the summand `z M` is type III\": it contains no\nnonzero finite projection.  (By Blackadar III.1.4.2 this is the defining\nfeature of type III; the equivalence with the full type classification is not\nformalized here.)\n-/\ndef SummandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) (z : H →L[ℂ] H) : Prop :=\n  ∀ e : H →L[ℂ] H, IsFiniteProjection M e → IsSubprojection e z → e = 0\n\n/-- A semifinite algebra, in the packet's central-summand sense, has no\ntype-III central summand: no nonzero central projection cuts out a summand\nwithout nonzero finite projections. -/\ntheorem not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection_of_isSemifinite\n    {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} (hM : IsSemifinite M) {z : H →L[ℂ] H}\n    (hz : IsCentralProjection M z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n    ¬ SummandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection M z := by\n  intro hno\n  obtain ⟨e, hefin, hene, hesub⟩ := hM z hz hz0\n  exact hene (hno e hefin hesub)\n\nend Abstract\n\nsection FiniteRange\n\nvariable {Site : Type*} [DecidableEq Site]\nvariable {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]\n\nopen scoped FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionQubitMatrix\n\nnamespace FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem\n\nvariable (R : FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem Site) {Q : QuasilocalEmbedding Site A}\nvariable (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q)\n\n/-! ### The unconditional theorem at the canonical algebra `M_Γ = π_ω(𝒜_loc)''` -/\n\n/--\n**The explicit finite witness in every nonzero central summand.**  For the GNS\nvon Neumann algebra `M_Γ = π_ω(𝒜_loc)''` of a supplied consistent finite-range\nstabilizer system, and any nonzero central projection `z`, the compression\n`z * q` of the constructed corner projection `q` is a nonzero finite projection\nof `M_Γ` lying below `z`.\n-/\ntheorem central_summand_finiteProjection_witness\n    (z : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS)\n    (hz : IsCentralProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n    IsFiniteProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra (z * R.cornerProjection W) ∧\n      z * R.cornerProjection W ≠ 0 ∧\n      IsSubprojection (z * R.cornerProjection W) z :=\n  (R.supportCornerConclusion_localVonNeumannAlgebra W).central_witness z hz hz0\n\n/--\n**The main theorem of the packet, central-summand form.**  Let `R` be a\nconsistent finite-range stabilizer system on a countable locally finite\nlattice, `Q` a quasilocal C-star completion of its finite local qubit algebras,\nand `W` a global stabilizer state extending the compatible finite local states.\nLet `M = M_Γ = π_ω(𝒜_loc)''` be the associated GNS von Neumann algebra.  Then\nfor every nonzero central projection `z` of `M`, the summand `z M` contains a\nnonzero finite projection.\n\nNo hypothesis beyond the supplied data `R`, `Q`, `W` is used.\n-/\ntheorem central_summand_exists_nonzero_finiteProjection\n    (z : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS)\n    (hz : IsCentralProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n    ∃ e : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS,\n      IsFiniteProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra e ∧ e ≠ 0 ∧ IsSubprojection e z :=\n  (R.supportCornerConclusion_localVonNeumannAlgebra W).semifinite z hz hz0\n\n/-- The same statement packaged as semifiniteness in the packet's\ncentral-summand sense. -/\ntheorem isSemifinite_localVonNeumannAlgebra :\n    IsSemifinite W.localVonNeumannAlgebra :=\n  (R.supportCornerConclusion_localVonNeumannAlgebra W).semifinite\n\n/--\n**No type-III central summand.**  For the GNS von Neumann algebra of a supplied\nconsistent finite-range stabilizer system, no nonzero central summand is purely\ninfinite in the projection sense; equivalently (Blackadar III.1.4.2, prose) no\nnonzero central summand is of type III.\n-/\ntheorem not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection\n    (z : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS)\n    (hz : IsCentralProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n    ¬ SummandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra z :=\n  not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection_of_isSemifinite\n    (R.isSemifinite_localVonNeumannAlgebra W) hz hz0\n\n/-- The corner projection is itself a nonzero finite projection of `M_Γ`: the\ncase `z = 1` of the central-summand theorem, recorded separately. -/\ntheorem cornerProjection_isFiniteProjection :\n    IsFiniteProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra (R.cornerProjection W) ∧\n      R.cornerProjection W ≠ 0 := by\n  have hone : IsCentralProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra 1 :=\n    ⟨⟨one_mem _, IsStarProjection.one _⟩, fun a _ => by rw [mul_one, one_mul]⟩\n  have hne : (1 : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS) ≠ 0 := by\n    intro h1\n    refine R.gnsVector_ne_zero W ?_\n    have : (1 : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS) W.gnsVector = (0 : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS) W.gnsVector := by\n      rw [h1]\n    simpa using this\n  have h := R.central_summand_finiteProjection_witness W 1 hone hne\n  rw [one_mul] at h\n  exact ⟨h.1, h.2.1⟩\n\n/-! ### The conditional theorem at a general von Neumann algebra\n\nThese variants keep the exact premises isolated by FF21 and FF22:\n`hM` (`M` contains the represented finite local algebras) and `hgen`\n(`M ⊆ π_ω(𝒜_loc)''`).  Together they say `M = M_Γ`.\n-/\n\nvariable (M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS)\nvariable (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n  W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M)\n\ninclude hM\n\n/--\n**Conditional central-summand theorem.**  For any von Neumann algebra `M` on\nthe GNS space which contains the represented finite local algebras (`hM`) and\nis contained in their bicommutant (`hgen`) — i.e. for `M = M_Γ` — every nonzero\ncentral summand of `M` contains a nonzero finite projection, with the explicit\nwitness `z * q`.\n-/\ntheorem central_summand_finiteProjection_witness_of_generated\n    (hgen : W.GeneratedByLocalAlgebra M)\n    (z : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS) (hz : IsCentralProjection M z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n    IsFiniteProjection M (z * R.cornerProjection W) ∧\n      z * R.cornerProjection W ≠ 0 ∧ IsSubprojection (z * R.cornerProjection W) z :=\n  (R.supportCornerConclusion W M hM hgen).central_witness z hz hz0\n\n/-- Conditional form: semifiniteness of `M` in the central-summand sense. -/\ntheorem isSemifinite_of_generated (hgen : W.GeneratedByLocalAlgebra M) :\n    IsSemifinite M :=\n  (R.supportCornerConclusion W M hM hgen).semifinite\n\n/-- Conditional form: no nonzero central summand of `M` is type III in the\nprojection sense. -/\ntheorem not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection_of_generated\n    (hgen : W.GeneratedByLocalAlgebra M)\n    (z : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS) (hz : IsCentralProjection M z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n    ¬ SummandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection M z :=\n  not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection_of_isSemifinite\n    (R.isSemifinite_of_generated W M hM hgen) hz hz0\n\nend FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem\n\nend FiniteRange\n\nend FiniteFiber\n--- remote summary ---\n# Summary of changes for run da7ae099-601d-45ab-9144-3aff6b76c5a7\n## FF23 delivered: `FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeNoTypeIII.lean`\n\nI read `manuscript/main.tex` and the checked FF20–FF22 layers (`ActualStabilizerSupportCorner.lean`, `FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction.lean`, `FiniteRangeTracialCorner.lean`) and created exactly one new Lean file, `FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeNoTypeIII.lean`, added to `FiniteFiber.lean`. It adds no new analytic input: it applies the already checked support-corner theorem to the concrete corner projection `q` constructed in FF21 and shown full/tracial/nonzero in FF22.\n\n### 1. Theorem recovered in the manuscript's intended form (unconditional relative to the supplied data)\n\nFor `R : FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem Site`, a quasilocal C*-completion `Q` and a global stabilizer state `W`, with `M_Γ = π_ω(𝒜_loc)'' = W.localVonNeumannAlgebra`:\n\n- `central_summand_exists_nonzero_finiteProjection` — for every nonzero central projection `z` of `M_Γ` there is a nonzero finite projection below `z` (the manuscript's `thm:finite_projections_exist`, central-summand form). **No hypothesis beyond `R`, `Q`, `W`.**\n- `central_summand_finiteProjection_witness` — the witness is explicitly `z * q`.\n- `isSemifinite_localVonNeumannAlgebra`, `cornerProjection_isFiniteProjection` (the `z = 1` case).\n- `not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection` — no nonzero central summand has the defining projection-level feature of type III, stated via the new definition `SummandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection`.\n\n### 2. Conditional theorem contract (exact extra premises preserved)\n\nFor a general von Neumann algebra `M` on the GNS space, the same conclusions are proved from exactly the FF21/FF22 premises, unchanged: `hM` (`M` contains the represented finite local algebras) and `hgen : W.GeneratedByLocalAlgebra M` (`M ⊆ 𝒜''`); together they say `M = M_Γ`, and they are discharged for the canonical algebra, which is why form 1 is unconditional. Theorems: `central_summand_finiteProjection_witness_of_generated`, `isSemifinite_of_generated`, `not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection_of_generated`.\n\n### 3. Prose corollary and remaining open items (clearly labelled)\n\nThe passage to \"no type-III factor in a standard central decomposition\" is written only as a labelled prose corollary in the module docstring (Blackadar III.1.4.2 plus the usual separability/measurable-field hypotheses); no direct-integral or fibrewise classification stat