{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/adversarial_review.md && printf '\\\\n--- exact changed-file contents ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeNoTypeIII.lean && tail -n 8 FiniteFiber.lean && printf '\\\\n--- dependency proof source ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1258,1274p' FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeTracialCorner.lean && printf '\\\\n--- current worktree target scope ---\\\\n' && git status --short -- FiniteFiber.lean FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeNoTypeIII.lean\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/adversarial_review.md && printf '\\\\n--- exact changed-file contents ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeNoTypeIII.lean && tail -n 8 FiniteFiber.lean && printf '\\\\n--- dependency proof source ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1258,1274p' FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeTracialCorner.lean && printf '\\\\n--- current worktree target scope ---\\\\n' && git status --short -- FiniteFiber.lean FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeNoTypeIII.lean\"","aggregated_output":"# Adversarial Review Protocol\n\nUse this before closing substantive Codex work. The goal is to find defects, not\nto summarize accomplishments.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. Identify the artifact types touched: `code`, `math`, `tex`, `computation`,\n   `source-backed`, `workflow`.\n2. Inspect the diff or new artifact against the user's request.\n3. Report findings by severity first. If there are no findings, say so and state\n   the remaining risk.\n\n## Universal Checks\n\n- Did the work answer the actual latest user request?\n- Did it modify unrelated files or broaden scope?\n- Did it overwrite, reformat, or revert pre-existing user changes?\n- Are generated files, caches, logs, plots, PDFs, or build artifacts handled\n  intentionally?\n- Are final claims stronger than the evidence supports?\n- Are verification commands actually relevant to the changed artifact?\n\n## Code Checks\n\n- Does the changed behavior match the stated interface and edge cases?\n- Are tests missing for a changed behavior, bug fix, parser, numerical routine,\n  CLI command, or user-facing workflow?\n- Are errors handled where inputs, files, network calls, or external tools can\n  fail?\n- Is there hidden global state, path sensitivity, nondeterminism, race risk, or\n  stale cache behavior?\n- Did dependency, config, or environment changes alter unrelated workflows?\n\n## Math Checks\n\n- Are all assumptions, domains, signs, conventions, normalizations, and boundary\n  conditions stated before use?\n- Are definitions used consistently throughout the derivation?\n- Is any implication actually reversible, or was a one-way statement used both\n  ways?\n- Are there division-by-zero, invertibility, regularity, convergence, branch-cut,\n  gauge, or boundary-term assumptions?\n- Do limiting cases, dimensions/units, symmetries, and known special cases agree?\n- Are symbolic substitutions justified rather than smuggling in the result?\n- Are claims labeled correctly as proof, derivation, check, conjecture, or\n  numerical evidence?\n\n## TeX And Source-Backed Checks\n\n- Does the document compile if compilation was expected?\n- Are labels, references, citations, bibliography entries, and figure paths valid?\n- Are source-backed claims tied to exact locators when required?\n- Is quoted or paraphrased material clearly separated from the agent's synthesis?\n- Does the exposition define terms before using them in load-bearing statements?\n\n## Computation Checks\n\n- Is the computation reproducible from a recorded command?\n- Are inputs, random seeds, versions, tolerances, and units documented when they\n  affect the result?\n- Are outputs interpreted correctly and not over-promoted beyond the computation?\n- Were independent sanity checks used where feasible: small cases, limiting\n  cases, dimensional analysis, symbolic identities, or alternate algorithms?\n\n## Closeout Template\n\nUse this structure internally, then surface the concise version to the user:\n\n```text\nFindings:\n- [severity] file/path:line - issue and consequence.\n\nChecks run:\n- command -> result.\n\nResidual risk:\n- what was not checked, or why the artifact is not a proof/complete validation.\n\nCleanup:\n- remaining dirty/untracked files and whether they are intentional.\n```\n\n--- exact changed-file contents ---\nimport FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeTracialCorner\n\n/-!\n# FF23 — finite-range stabilizer systems have no type-III central summand\n\nFor supplied finite-range stabilizer data, a quasilocal completion, and a\nglobal stabilizer state, this module applies the FF20--FF22 support-corner\nconclusion at the canonical GNS von Neumann algebra.  It proves the exact\ncentral-summand form: every nonzero central projection has a nonzero finite\nsubprojection.  The quasilocal completion and global state remain supplied\ndata; no direct-integral or fibrewise type-classification claim is formalized.\n\nUnder the usual separability and central-decomposition hypotheses, the\ncentral-summand conclusion excludes type-III factor fibres.  That implication\nis prose only: the requisite direct-integral API is not developed here.\n-/\n\nnamespace FiniteFiber\n\nsection Abstract\n\nvariable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n\n/-- The projection-level absence-of-finiteness property for a central summand. -/\ndef SummandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) (z : H →L[ℂ] H) : Prop :=\n  ∀ e : H →L[ℂ] H, IsFiniteProjection M e → IsSubprojection e z → e = 0\n\n/-- Semifiniteness in the packet's central-summand sense rules out the displayed\nabsence-of-finiteness property in each nonzero central summand. -/\ntheorem not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection_of_isSemifinite\n    {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} (hM : IsSemifinite M) {z : H →L[ℂ] H}\n    (hz : IsCentralProjection M z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n    ¬ SummandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection M z := by\n  intro hno\n  obtain ⟨e, hefin, hene, hesub⟩ := hM z hz hz0\n  exact hene (hno e hefin hesub)\n\nend Abstract\n\nsection FiniteRange\n\nvariable {Site : Type*} [DecidableEq Site]\nvariable {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]\n\nopen scoped FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionQubitMatrix\n\nnamespace FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem\n\nvariable (R : FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem Site) {Q : QuasilocalEmbedding Site A}\nvariable (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q)\n\n/-- For every nonzero central projection of the canonical GNS von Neumann\nalgebra, `z * q` is a nonzero finite projection below `z`. -/\ntheorem central_summand_finiteProjection_witness\n    (z : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS)\n    (hz : IsCentralProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n    IsFiniteProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra (z * R.cornerProjection W) ∧\n      z * R.cornerProjection W ≠ 0 ∧\n      IsSubprojection (z * R.cornerProjection W) z :=\n  (R.supportCornerConclusion_localVonNeumannAlgebra W).central_witness z hz hz0\n\n/-- The FF23 central-summand theorem at the canonical GNS von Neumann algebra. -/\ntheorem central_summand_exists_nonzero_finiteProjection\n    (z : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS)\n    (hz : IsCentralProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n    ∃ e : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS,\n      IsFiniteProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra e ∧ e ≠ 0 ∧ IsSubprojection e z :=\n  (R.supportCornerConclusion_localVonNeumannAlgebra W).semifinite z hz hz0\n\n/-- The canonical GNS von Neumann algebra is semifinite in the packet's\ncentral-summand sense. -/\ntheorem isSemifinite_localVonNeumannAlgebra :\n    IsSemifinite W.localVonNeumannAlgebra :=\n  (R.supportCornerConclusion_localVonNeumannAlgebra W).semifinite\n\n/-- No nonzero central summand of the canonical GNS algebra has no nonzero\nfinite subprojection. -/\ntheorem not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection\n    (z : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS)\n    (hz : IsCentralProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n    ¬ SummandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra z :=\n  not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection_of_isSemifinite\n    (R.isSemifinite_localVonNeumannAlgebra W) hz hz0\n\n/-- The concrete corner is a nonzero finite projection of the canonical GNS\nvon Neumann algebra. -/\ntheorem cornerProjection_isFiniteProjection :\n    IsFiniteProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra (R.cornerProjection W) ∧\n      R.cornerProjection W ≠ 0 := by\n  have hone : IsCentralProjection W.localVonNeumannAlgebra 1 :=\n    ⟨⟨one_mem _, IsStarProjection.one _⟩, fun a _ => by rw [mul_one, one_mul]⟩\n  have hne : (1 : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS) ≠ 0 := by\n    intro h1\n    refine R.gnsVector_ne_zero W ?_\n    have : (1 : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS) W.gnsVector = (0 : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS) W.gnsVector := by\n      rw [h1]\n    simpa using this\n  have h := R.central_summand_finiteProjection_witness W 1 hone hne\n  rw [one_mul] at h\n  exact ⟨h.1, h.2.1⟩\n\nvariable (M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS)\nvariable (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n  W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M)\n\ninclude hM\n\n/-- The same explicit witness for a supplied algebra identified with the local\nbicommutant by containment and generation hypotheses. -/\ntheorem central_summand_finiteProjection_witness_of_generated\n    (hgen : W.GeneratedByLocalAlgebra M)\n    (z : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS) (hz : IsCentralProjection M z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n    IsFiniteProjection M (z * R.cornerProjection W) ∧\n      z * R.cornerProjection W ≠ 0 ∧ IsSubprojection (z * R.cornerProjection W) z :=\n  (R.supportCornerConclusion W M hM hgen).central_witness z hz hz0\n\n/-- Conditional central-summand semifiniteness for a general presented algebra. -/\ntheorem isSemifinite_of_generated (hgen : W.GeneratedByLocalAlgebra M) :\n    IsSemifinite M :=\n  (R.supportCornerConclusion W M hM hgen).semifinite\n\n/-- Conditional absence-of-finiteness exclusion for a general presented algebra. -/\ntheorem not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection_of_generated\n    (hgen : W.GeneratedByLocalAlgebra M)\n    (z : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS) (hz : IsCentralProjection M z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n    ¬ SummandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection M z :=\n  not_summandHasNoNonzeroFiniteProjection_of_isSemifinite\n    (R.isSemifinite_of_generated W M hM hgen) hz hz0\n\nend FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem\n\nend FiniteRange\n\nend FiniteFiber\nimport FiniteFiber.FiniteNestedTensorState\nimport FiniteFiber.FiniteStabilizerStateChain\nimport FiniteFiber.SequentialLocalFunctional\nimport FiniteFiber.CountablePauliRepresentation\nimport FiniteFiber.ActualStabilizerSupportCorner\nimport FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction\nimport FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeTracialCorner\nimport FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeNoTypeIII\n\n--- dependency proof source ---\n/--\n**The main theorem of this packet.**  For a finite-range consistent stabilizer system on a\ncountable locally finite lattice, a quasilocal completion `Q` and its global stabilizer\nstate `W`, the canonical corner projection `q` of the represented local code-space supports\nis a nonzero full projection of the manuscript's algebra `M_Γ = π_ω(𝒜_loc)''`, the corner\nvector state `τ_q` is a faithful tracial state on `q M_Γ q`, and the whole\n`SupportCornerConclusion` of FF20 holds — with **no** additional hypothesis.\n\n(The no-type-III conclusion is *not* asserted here; that is FF23.)\n-/\ntheorem supportCornerConclusion_localVonNeumannAlgebra :\n    SupportCornerConclusion W.localVonNeumannAlgebra (R.cornerProjection W) W.gnsVector :=\n  R.supportCornerConclusion W W.localVonNeumannAlgebra\n    W.representation_mem_localVonNeumannAlgebra\n    W.generatedByLocalAlgebra_localVonNeumannAlgebra\n\nend FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem\n\n--- current worktree target scope ---\n?? FiniteFiber.lean\n?? FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeNoTypeIII.lean\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
